From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:18:40 -0400
Subject: look: a neutral palette with no amber, and the command bar's rows
 under the pointer

The active Space's colour reached the window as Chromium's user colour
marked as an accent, so Chromium generated its whole Material palette
from it: a warm Space turned Settings, menus, toggles and the command
bar's chip brown and orange. The colour now keeps tinting the sidebar's
ground and nothing else; the rest of the window keeps Chromium's
baseline palette, as a window with no Space colour has (spaces B11).

The light look's ground, a sand, is Tailwind's slate-300, and the
welcome page's sand and amber are Tailwind's slate scale (welcome W15,
VISION's visual direction). The mark's amber dot stays for now.

A command bar row under the pointer shows a ground, fainter than the
chosen row's; the pointer never moves the choice (commandbar K37).

Why: the owner, 2026-10-26 (no amber anywhere; rows gave no sign under
the pointer).
Removable when: never; to be folded into the patches that own the code.
